  "interpretation": "Camera-by-component heterogeneity is scientifically useful: the block space materially improves observation p90 over the v182 global residual line and recovers 37 of 52 all-nine cells. It remains insufficient because observation p90 still exceeds the frozen 0.20 gate under both sensor arms.",
  "limitation": "This closes only the frozen exact one-coefficient-per-camera-component Galerkin mechanism on a post-open four-frame straight-ray PoolFire proxy. It is not an impossibility result for the C route and establishes no deployment, resource, external, curved-ray, or real-BOST result.",
